## 1. Architecture Overview

```
                 Corporate Network (air-gapped)
 ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │                                                                │
 │  ┌──────────┐   ┌──────────────┐   ┌─────────────────────────┐ │
 │  │ Bastion  │   │ Mirror       │   │ External Load Balancer  │ │
 │  │ (RHEL 9) │   │ Registry     │   │ API :6443  MCS :22623   │ │
 │  │ oc, oc-  │   │ (Quay)       │   │ Ingress :80 / :443      │ │
 │  │ mirror   │   │ :8443        │   └────────────┬────────────┘ │
 │  └──────────┘   └──────────────┘                │              │
 │                                                 │              │
 │  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┴────────────┐ │
 │  │  master-0   master-1   master-2        (Control plane)   │ │
 │  │  infra-0    infra-1    infra-2         (Router/Mon/Log)  │ │
 │  │  worker-0   worker-1   worker-N        (Applications)    │ │
 │  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
 │   DNS · NTP · DHCP(optional) · ODF/CSI storage                 │
 └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Design decisions**

| Item | Choice | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| Installer | Agent-based installer | Red Hat recommended for disconnected bare metal; no bootstrap node needed |
| Control plane | 3 nodes, unschedulable | etcd quorum; isolate platform |
| Infra nodes | 3 nodes | Router, registry, monitoring, logging off worker subscriptions |
| Workers | 3+ | Sized to workload; scale later |
| CNI | OVN-Kubernetes | Default and only supported SDN going forward |
| Storage | LSO + ODF (internal mode) | Block, file, object on local disks |
| Node OS | RHCOS | Managed by Machine Config Operator |
| FIPS | Decide at install | Cannot be changed post-install |

