## 2. Prerequisites

### 2.1 Hardware (minimum production)

| Role | Qty | vCPU | RAM | OS Disk | Data Disks | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Control plane | 3 | 8 | 32 GB | 200 GB NVMe/SSD | — | etcd fsync p99 < 10 ms |
| Infra | 3 | 8 | 32 GB | 200 GB SSD | 2–4 × 1–2 TB SSD (ODF) | Also hosts ODF if co-located |
| Worker | 3+ | 16 | 64 GB | 200 GB SSD | per workload | |
| Bastion | 1 | 4 | 16 GB | 500 GB | — | Hosts mirror registry (~500 GB–1 TB for images) |

- All nodes: UEFI boot, BMC with Redfish/IPMI, virtual-media support (for ISO boot), PXE optional.
- Two NICs per node recommended (bonded) with LACP on the switch.
- Record **MAC addresses** of the provisioning NIC for every node — required for `agent-config.yaml`.

### 2.2 Network

| Network | Example CIDR | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Machine network | `192.168.100.0/24` | Node IPs; must be routable to LB, DNS, NTP, registry |
| Cluster (pod) network | `10.128.0.0/14`, hostPrefix 23 | Must not overlap corporate ranges |
| Service network | `172.30.0.0/16` | Must not overlap |
| API VIP | `192.168.100.5` | Only if using built-in keepalived; otherwise LB address |
| Ingress VIP | `192.168.100.6` | Same as above |

**Firewall ports (node-to-node):** TCP 2379–2380 (etcd, masters), 6443, 22623, 10250–10259, 9000–9999, 30000–32767; UDP 6081 (Geneve/OVN), 500/4500 (IPsec if enabled), 123 (NTP).
**Firewall ports (external → cluster):** TCP 6443 (API), 22623 (MCS, internal only), 80/443 (ingress).
**Cluster → mirror registry:** TCP 8443 (or chosen port).

### 2.3 DNS records (mandatory)

```
api.ocp-prod.example.com.        IN A    192.168.100.5   ; LB / API VIP
api-int.ocp-prod.example.com.    IN A    192.168.100.5   ; LB / API VIP
*.apps.ocp-prod.example.com.     IN A    192.168.100.6   ; LB / Ingress VIP
master-0.ocp-prod.example.com.   IN A    192.168.100.10
master-1.ocp-prod.example.com.   IN A    192.168.100.11
master-2.ocp-prod.example.com.   IN A    192.168.100.12
infra-0.ocp-prod.example.com.    IN A    192.168.100.20
infra-1.ocp-prod.example.com.    IN A    192.168.100.21
infra-2.ocp-prod.example.com.    IN A    192.168.100.22
worker-0.ocp-prod.example.com.   IN A    192.168.100.30
worker-1.ocp-prod.example.com.   IN A    192.168.100.31
worker-2.ocp-prod.example.com.   IN A    192.168.100.32
registry.example.com.            IN A    192.168.100.2   ; mirror registry
bastion.example.com.             IN A    192.168.100.2
```
Create matching **PTR** records for every node.

Verify from bastion:
```bash
for h in api api-int master-0 infra-0 worker-0; do dig +short ${h}.ocp-prod.example.com; done
dig +short test.apps.ocp-prod.example.com
dig +short -x 192.168.100.10
```

### 2.4 External load balancer (HAProxy example)

```haproxy
global
    log /dev/log local0
    maxconn 20000
defaults
    mode tcp
    log global
    option tcplog
    timeout connect 10s
    timeout client 1m
    timeout server 1m

frontend api        bind *:6443
    default_backend api
backend api
    balance roundrobin
    option httpchk GET /readyz HTTP/1.0
    option log-health-checks
    server master-0 192.168.100.10:6443 check check-ssl inter 1s fall 2 rise 3 verify none
    server master-1 192.168.100.11:6443 check check-ssl inter 1s fall 2 rise 3 verify none
    server master-2 192.168.100.12:6443 check check-ssl inter 1s fall 2 rise 3 verify none

frontend mcs        bind *:22623
    default_backend mcs
backend mcs
    balance roundrobin
    server master-0 192.168.100.10:22623 check inter 1s
    server master-1 192.168.100.11:22623 check inter 1s
    server master-2 192.168.100.12:22623 check inter 1s

frontend ingress-http   bind *:80
    default_backend ingress-http
backend ingress-http
    balance source
    server infra-0 192.168.100.20:80 check inter 1s
    server infra-1 192.168.100.21:80 check inter 1s
    server infra-2 192.168.100.22:80 check inter 1s

frontend ingress-https  bind *:443
    default_backend ingress-https
backend ingress-https
    balance source
    server infra-0 192.168.100.20:443 check inter 1s
    server infra-1 192.168.100.21:443 check inter 1s
    server infra-2 192.168.100.22:443 check inter 1s
```
Deploy HAProxy as an **HA pair** (keepalived) or use an enterprise LB (F5, Citrix). Port 22623 must **not** be reachable from outside the cluster network.

### 2.5 NTP
All nodes must reach an internal NTP server. Record the server IP for the chrony MachineConfig (Section 8.2).

### 2.6 Accounts and artifacts to collect

- Red Hat account with OpenShift subscription; download **pull secret** from `https://console.redhat.com/openshift/install/pull-secret`.
- Enterprise CA certificate chain (PEM) if the mirror registry cert is enterprise-signed.
- An internet-connected staging host (temporary) for downloading tools and mirroring images, plus a method to transfer data into the air-gapped network (removable media or a one-way transfer).

