## 4. Mirror Registry Setup

Red Hat's `mirror-registry` deploys a minimal, supported Quay instance on the bastion.

### 4.1 Install

```bash
mkdir -p /opt/quay && cd ~/ocp-tools
tar xzf mirror-registry.tar.gz -C /opt/quay
cd /opt/quay

sudo ./mirror-registry install \
  --quayHostname registry.example.com \
  --quayRoot /opt/quay/data \
  --quayStorage /opt/quay/storage \
  --initUser admin \
  --initPassword 'ChangeMe-StrongPassword!' \
  --sslCert   /path/to/registry.example.com.crt \   # optional: enterprise cert
  --sslKey    /path/to/registry.example.com.key
```
If you omit `--sslCert/--sslKey`, a self-signed CA is generated at `/opt/quay/data/quay-rootCA/rootCA.pem`.

### 4.2 Trust the registry CA on the bastion

```bash
sudo cp /opt/quay/data/quay-rootCA/rootCA.pem /etc/pki/ca-trust/source/anchors/registry-ca.pem
sudo update-ca-trust
podman login -u admin registry.example.com:8443
```

### 4.3 Merge registry credentials into the pull secret

```bash
REG_AUTH=$(echo -n 'admin:ChangeMe-StrongPassword!' | base64 -w0)
jq --arg a "$REG_AUTH" '.auths["registry.example.com:8443"] = {"auth": $a, "email": "admin@example.com"}' \
   pull-secret.json > pull-secret-merged.json
cp pull-secret-merged.json ~/.docker/config.json
```

### 4.4 Validate

```bash
curl -k https://registry.example.com:8443/health/instance
podman pull registry.example.com:8443/... (after mirroring)
```

Enable the systemd services so Quay survives reboot (`mirror-registry` does this by default; verify with `systemctl status quay-app quay-postgres quay-redis`).

