## 5. Mirroring Release and Operator Images (oc-mirror)

Use **oc-mirror v2** (`--v2`). Mirroring is done on the connected host to disk, transferred, then pushed to the mirror registry.

### 5.1 Discover available operators **[connected]**

```bash
oc-mirror list operators --catalog registry.redhat.io/redhat/redhat-operator-index:v4.22
oc-mirror list operators --catalog registry.redhat.io/redhat/redhat-operator-index:v4.22 --package odf-operator
```

### 5.2 ImageSetConfiguration

Save as `imageset-config.yaml`. Adjust channels/versions to your target release.

```yaml
kind: ImageSetConfiguration
apiVersion: mirror.openshift.io/v2alpha1
mirror:
  platform:
    channels:
      - name: eus-4.22          # or stable-4.22
        minVersion: 4.22.16
        maxVersion: 4.22.16
        shortestPath: true
    graph: true               # required for OSUS (disconnected update graph)

  operators:
    - catalog: registry.redhat.io/redhat/redhat-operator-index:v4.22
      packages:
        # --- Storage ---
        - name: local-storage-operator
        - name: odf-operator
        - name: ocs-operator
        - name: mcg-operator
        - name: odf-csi-addons-operator
        - name: odf-prometheus-operator
        - name: recipe
        - name: rook-ceph-operator
        - name: cephcsi-operator
        # --- Logging / Observability ---
        - name: cluster-logging
        - name: loki-operator
        - name: cluster-observability-operator
        - name: opentelemetry-product
        - name: tempo-product
        # --- Security / Compliance ---
        - name: compliance-operator
        - name: file-integrity-operator
        - name: security-profiles-operator
        - name: rhacs-operator
        # --- Certificates / Secrets ---
        - name: openshift-cert-manager-operator
        # --- GitOps / CI ---
        - name: openshift-gitops-operator
        - name: openshift-pipelines-operator-rh
        # --- Networking ---
        - name: metallb-operator
        - name: kubernetes-nmstate-operator
        # --- Nodes ---
        - name: nfd
        - name: node-maintenance-operator
        - name: kernel-module-management
        # --- Backup / Updates / Fleet ---
        - name: redhat-oadp-operator
        - name: cincinnati-operator          # OpenShift Update Service (OSUS)
        - name: advanced-cluster-management   # optional
        - name: multicluster-engine           # required by ACM
        - name: cluster-resource-override-operator
    - catalog: registry.redhat.io/redhat/certified-operator-index:v4.22
      packages:
        - name: external-secrets-operator     # verify exact package name
    - catalog: registry.redhat.io/redhat/community-operator-index:v4.22
      packages: []                            # add only if a community operator is approved

  additionalImages:
    - name: registry.redhat.io/ubi9/ubi:latest
    - name: registry.redhat.io/rhel9/support-tools:latest
    - name: registry.redhat.io/openshift4/ose-tools-rhel9:latest

  helm: {}
```

> Operator package names and dependencies change between releases. Run `oc-mirror list operators --catalog ... --package <name>` to confirm each name and its default channel before mirroring.

### 5.3 Mirror to disk **[connected]**

```bash
mkdir -p ~/mirror-data
oc-mirror --v2 -c imageset-config.yaml file://~/mirror-data --authfile ~/.docker/config.json
```
Expect 100–400 GB depending on operator list. Verify the archive(s) `mirror_000001.tar ...` were created.

### 5.4 Transfer and push to the mirror registry **[bastion]**

```bash
oc-mirror --v2 -c imageset-config.yaml \
  --from file:///data/mirror-data \
  docker://registry.example.com:8443 \
  --authfile ~/.docker/config.json
```

oc-mirror writes cluster resources to `mirror-data/working-dir/cluster-resources/`:

- `idms-oc-mirror.yaml` — ImageDigestMirrorSet
- `itms-oc-mirror.yaml` — ImageTagMirrorSet
- `cs-redhat-operator-index-v4-22.yaml` — CatalogSource(s)
- `updateService.yaml` — for OSUS (when `graph: true`)
- `signature-configmap.yaml` — release signatures

Keep these; they are applied in Section 7.

### 5.5 Extract values needed for install-config

```bash
cat mirror-data/working-dir/cluster-resources/idms-oc-mirror.yaml
# Note the 'source' → 'mirrors' pairs for:
#   quay.io/openshift-release-dev/ocp-release
#   quay.io/openshift-release-dev/ocp-v4.0-art-dev
```

