## 6. Cluster Installation (Agent-Based Installer)

### 6.1 Working directory

```bash
mkdir -p ~/ocp-prod && cd ~/ocp-prod
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -N '' -f ~/.ssh/ocp-prod
```

### 6.2 `install-config.yaml`

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
baseDomain: example.com
metadata:
  name: ocp-prod
fips: false                              # set true BEFORE install if required
compute:
  - name: worker
    replicas: 6                          # 3 infra + 3 worker (infra are labelled post-install)
    architecture: amd64
    hyperthreading: Enabled
controlPlane:
  name: master
  replicas: 3
  architecture: amd64
  hyperthreading: Enabled
networking:
  networkType: OVNKubernetes
  clusterNetwork:
    - cidr: 10.128.0.0/14
      hostPrefix: 23
  serviceNetwork:
    - 172.30.0.0/16
  machineNetwork:
    - cidr: 192.168.100.0/24
platform:
  baremetal:
    apiVIPs:
      - 192.168.100.5
    ingressVIPs:
      - 192.168.100.6
# Use `platform: none: {}` instead of baremetal if ALL traffic goes through the external LB
# and you do not want the in-cluster keepalived/haproxy VIPs.
pullSecret: '<CONTENTS OF pull-secret-merged.json, single line>'
sshKey: '<CONTENTS OF ~/.ssh/ocp-prod.pub>'
additionalTrustBundlePolicy: Always
additionalTrustBundle: |
  -----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----
  <mirror registry root CA PEM — indented 2 spaces>
  -----END CERTIFICATE-----
imageDigestSources:
  - mirrors:
      - registry.example.com:8443/openshift/release
    source: quay.io/openshift-release-dev/ocp-v4.0-art-dev
  - mirrors:
      - registry.example.com:8443/openshift/release-images
    source: quay.io/openshift-release-dev/ocp-release
```

> Copy the exact `mirrors`/`source` values from `idms-oc-mirror.yaml` generated by oc-mirror.

### 6.3 `agent-config.yaml`

Static IPs via NMState are strongly recommended for production. Repeat the `hosts` block for every node.

```yaml
apiVersion: v1beta1
kind: AgentConfig
metadata:
  name: ocp-prod
rendezvousIP: 192.168.100.10          # must be one of the control-plane node IPs
additionalNTPSources:
  - ntp.example.com
hosts:
  - hostname: master-0
    role: master
    rootDeviceHints:
      deviceName: /dev/nvme0n1          # or wwn/serial for determinism
    interfaces:
      - name: eno1
        macAddress: AA:BB:CC:00:10:01
      - name: eno2
        macAddress: AA:BB:CC:00:10:02
    networkConfig:
      interfaces:
        - name: bond0
          type: bond
          state: up
          ipv4:
            enabled: true
            address:
              - ip: 192.168.100.10
                prefix-length: 24
            dhcp: false
          link-aggregation:
            mode: 802.3ad
            options:
              miimon: "100"
            port:
              - eno1
              - eno2
      dns-resolver:
        config:
          server:
            - 192.168.100.3
          search:
            - ocp-prod.example.com
      routes:
        config:
          - destination: 0.0.0.0/0
            next-hop-address: 192.168.100.1
            next-hop-interface: bond0
            table-id: 254
  - hostname: master-1
    role: master
    # ...same structure, IP 192.168.100.11
  - hostname: master-2
    role: master
    # ...IP 192.168.100.12
  - hostname: infra-0
    role: worker
    # ...IP 192.168.100.20
  - hostname: infra-1
    role: worker
  - hostname: infra-2
    role: worker
  - hostname: worker-0
    role: worker
    # ...IP 192.168.100.30
  - hostname: worker-1
    role: worker
  - hostname: worker-2
    role: worker
```

### 6.4 (Optional) Day-0 custom manifests

Place extra manifests in `~/ocp-prod/openshift/` before generating the ISO (e.g., chrony config, kernel args, disabling default OperatorHub sources). Example — chrony for workers (generate via butane):

```yaml
# 99-worker-chrony.bu
variant: openshift
version: 4.22.0
metadata:
  name: 99-worker-chrony
  labels:
    machineconfiguration.openshift.io/role: worker
storage:
  files:
    - path: /etc/chrony.conf
      mode: 0644
      overwrite: true
      contents:
        inline: |
          server ntp.example.com iburst
          driftfile /var/lib/chrony/drift
          makestep 1.0 3
          rtcsync
          logdir /var/log/chrony
```
```bash
butane 99-worker-chrony.bu -o openshift/99-worker-chrony.yaml
sed 's/worker/master/g' 99-worker-chrony.bu | butane -o openshift/99-master-chrony.yaml
```

### 6.5 Generate the agent ISO

```bash
cd ~/ocp-prod
cp install-config.yaml agent-config.yaml ~/ocp-prod-backup/   # the installer consumes them
openshift-install agent create image --dir . --log-level=info
ls -lh agent.x86_64.iso auth/
```
`auth/kubeconfig` and `auth/kubeadmin-password` are generated now — protect them.

### 6.6 Boot the nodes

1. Upload `agent.x86_64.iso` to a web server reachable by the BMCs, or attach directly via virtual media.
2. For every node, mount the ISO via Redfish virtual media and set one-time boot to CD:
   ```bash
   # Example (Dell iDRAC/Redfish); adjust for your vendor or use the BMC UI
   curl -k -u user:pass -X POST \
     https://<bmc-ip>/redfish/v1/Managers/iDRAC.Embedded.1/VirtualMedia/CD/Actions/VirtualMedia.InsertMedia \
     -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"Image":"http://bastion.example.com/agent.x86_64.iso"}'
   curl -k -u user:pass -X PATCH https://<bmc-ip>/redfish/v1/Systems/System.Embedded.1 \
     -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
     -d '{"Boot":{"BootSourceOverrideTarget":"Cd","BootSourceOverrideEnabled":"Once"}}'
   curl -k -u user:pass -X POST https://<bmc-ip>/redfish/v1/Systems/System.Embedded.1/Actions/ComputerSystem.Reset \
     -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"ResetType":"ForceRestart"}'
   ```
3. Boot the **rendezvous node (master-0) first**, then the remaining nodes within a few minutes.

### 6.7 Monitor installation

```bash
openshift-install agent wait-for bootstrap-complete --dir . --log-level=info
# ~20–40 min. Then:
openshift-install agent wait-for install-complete --dir . --log-level=info
```

In parallel (optional), check the assisted-service UI on the rendezvous node: `http://192.168.100.10:8090` and SSH: `ssh -i ~/.ssh/ocp-prod core@192.168.100.10` → `journalctl -u assisted-service -f`.

### 6.8 First login and verification

```bash
export KUBECONFIG=~/ocp-prod/auth/kubeconfig
oc get nodes
oc get clusterversion
oc get co                      # all AVAILABLE=True, PROGRESSING=False, DEGRADED=False
oc get csr -o name | xargs oc adm certificate approve   # if any pending
oc get pods -A | grep -vE 'Running|Completed'
```

