## 7. Post-Install: Disconnected Registry Configuration

### 7.1 Apply oc-mirror generated resources

```bash
cd ~/mirror-data/working-dir/cluster-resources
oc apply -f idms-oc-mirror.yaml
oc apply -f itms-oc-mirror.yaml
oc apply -f signature-configmap.yaml
oc apply -f cs-redhat-operator-index-v4-22.yaml
oc apply -f cs-certified-operator-index-v4-22.yaml   # if mirrored
```
Applying IDMS/ITMS triggers a rolling MachineConfig update — wait for it: `oc get mcp -w`.

### 7.2 Disable default (internet) OperatorHub sources

```bash
oc patch OperatorHub cluster --type merge -p '{"spec":{"disableAllDefaultSources":true}}'
oc get catalogsource -n openshift-marketplace
oc get packagemanifests | head
```

### 7.3 Trust the mirror registry cluster-wide (if not done via install-config)

```bash
oc create configmap registry-ca -n openshift-config \
  --from-file=registry.example.com..8443=/opt/quay/data/quay-rootCA/rootCA.pem
oc patch image.config.openshift.io/cluster --type merge \
  -p '{"spec":{"additionalTrustedCA":{"name":"registry-ca"}}}'
```

### 7.4 OpenShift Update Service (OSUS) for disconnected upgrades

```bash
oc create ns openshift-update-service
# Install cincinnati-operator (see Section 9 pattern), then:
oc apply -f updateService.yaml          # generated by oc-mirror
# Point CVO at the local graph:
oc patch clusterversion version --type merge -p \
  '{"spec":{"upstream":"https://<osus-route>/api/upgrades_info/graph","channel":"eus-4.22"}}'
oc adm upgrade
```

