## 8. Post-Install: Cluster Configuration

### 8.1 Infra nodes

```bash
for n in infra-0 infra-1 infra-2; do
  oc label node $n node-role.kubernetes.io/infra=""
  oc label node $n node-role.kubernetes.io/worker-   # remove worker role label
  oc adm taint node $n node-role.kubernetes.io/infra=reserved:NoSchedule
  oc adm taint node $n node-role.kubernetes.io/infra=reserved:NoExecute
done
```

Create an infra MachineConfigPool so MCO manages them separately:
```yaml
apiVersion: machineconfiguration.openshift.io/v1
kind: MachineConfigPool
metadata:
  name: infra
spec:
  machineConfigSelector:
    matchExpressions:
      - key: machineconfiguration.openshift.io/role
        operator: In
        values: [worker, infra]
  nodeSelector:
    matchLabels:
      node-role.kubernetes.io/infra: ""
```

Move platform components to infra:

```bash
# Ingress
oc patch ingresscontroller default -n openshift-ingress-operator --type merge -p \
'{"spec":{"replicas":3,"nodePlacement":{"nodeSelector":{"matchLabels":{"node-role.kubernetes.io/infra":""}},
"tolerations":[{"key":"node-role.kubernetes.io/infra","value":"reserved","effect":"NoSchedule"},
{"key":"node-role.kubernetes.io/infra","value":"reserved","effect":"NoExecute"}]}}}'

# Image registry
oc patch configs.imageregistry.operator.openshift.io/cluster --type merge -p \
'{"spec":{"nodeSelector":{"node-role.kubernetes.io/infra":""},
"tolerations":[{"key":"node-role.kubernetes.io/infra","value":"reserved","effect":"NoSchedule"},
{"key":"node-role.kubernetes.io/infra","value":"reserved","effect":"NoExecute"}]}}'
```

Monitoring (see 8.5 ConfigMap — includes nodeSelector/tolerations).

### 8.2 Control plane unschedulable & chrony (if not done day-0)

```bash
oc patch schedulers.config.openshift.io cluster --type merge -p '{"spec":{"mastersSchedulable":false}}'
oc apply -f openshift/99-master-chrony.yaml -f openshift/99-worker-chrony.yaml
```

### 8.3 Storage: Local Storage Operator + ODF

Install `local-storage-operator` (ns `openshift-local-storage`) and `odf-operator` (ns `openshift-storage`) via Section 9, then:

```bash
oc label node infra-0 infra-1 infra-2 cluster.ocs.openshift.io/openshift-storage=""
```
```yaml
apiVersion: local.storage.openshift.io/v1alpha1
kind: LocalVolumeSet
metadata:
  name: odf-disks
  namespace: openshift-local-storage
spec:
  nodeSelector:
    nodeSelectorTerms:
      - matchExpressions:
          - key: cluster.ocs.openshift.io/openshift-storage
            operator: In
            values: [""]
  storageClassName: localblock
  volumeMode: Block
  deviceInclusionSpec:
    deviceTypes: [disk]
    deviceMechanicalProperties: [NonRotational]
    minSize: 500Gi
  tolerations:
    - key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra
      value: reserved
      effect: NoSchedule
    - key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra
      value: reserved
      effect: NoExecute
```
```yaml
apiVersion: ocs.openshift.io/v1
kind: StorageCluster
metadata:
  name: ocs-storagecluster
  namespace: openshift-storage
spec:
  manageNodes: false
  resources: {}
  monDataDirHostPath: /var/lib/rook
  placement:
    all:
      tolerations:
        - key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra
          value: reserved
          effect: NoSchedule
        - key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra
          value: reserved
          effect: NoExecute
  storageDeviceSets:
    - name: ocs-deviceset
      count: 1                      # number of disks per node
      replica: 3
      portable: false
      dataPVCTemplate:
        spec:
          storageClassName: localblock
          accessModes: [ReadWriteOnce]
          volumeMode: Block
          resources:
            requests:
              storage: "1"
```
Verify: `oc get storagecluster -n openshift-storage`, `oc get sc` (expect `ocs-storagecluster-ceph-rbd`, `-cephfs`, `openshift-storage.noobaa.io`). Set a default StorageClass:
```bash
oc patch sc ocs-storagecluster-ceph-rbd -p '{"metadata":{"annotations":{"storageclass.kubernetes.io/is-default-class":"true"}}}'
```
